# adjacency_spacetransform

- Label: Space Transform with Adjacency
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 2 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/adjacency_spacetransform.html
- Summary (EN): Re-expresses a world-space vector in tangent space, the parametrization of the tangent plane fitted to a 3D surface. It is used when a geometry's vectors need to point in a specific direction.
- Résumé (FR) : Exprime un vecteur monde dans l'espace tangent de la surface, avec un câble d'adjacence obligatoire.

- Inputs meaning: ["coord: world-space vector to transform, supplied as an RGB vector", "adjacency: adjacency cable from a Geometry to Adjacency COP"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: output layer type; RGB keeps the full vector, UV keeps only X and Y", "Transformation: the only option is World to Tangent"]

- Caveats: ["The adjacency input is mandatory and must come from a Geometry to Adjacency COP", "Choosing UV drops the Z component of the vector", "Only world-to-tangent conversion is offered", "The page text does not state the internal name; the match relies on the page icon and the node index link", "Results are best when the target texture matches the rasterized adjacency maps", "Introduced in Houdini 22.0"]

